00:54:44.540 --> 00:54:50.400
know, labor laws notwithstanding, used?
I guess I can take that one. So there has

00:54:50.400 --> 00:54:58.500
been a large number of what's called cross-fostering
experiments, and I'm nowhere familiar with

00:54:58.500 --> 00:55:03.090
all of that literature. But what typically
happens is that unless you're actually giving

00:55:03.090 --> 00:55:10.210
a human child to another human ... And let's
remember that there really are, genetically

00:55:10.210 --> 00:55:16.130
speaking, no races, so it's just a member
of the same species, okay? That's not cross-fostering.

00:55:16.130 --> 00:55:25.359
But for instance, if you raise a canary among
zebra finches, the canary will try to learn

00:55:25.359 --> 00:55:31.080
to sing like a zebra finch that has a very
different song. And at some level, it will

00:55:31.080 --> 00:55:36.871
acquire many of the elements of their song,
and it will fail to acquire others because

00:55:36.871 --> 00:55:44.069
at some level there's a breakdown in how matched
their hardware can imitate the, you know ... Canaries

00:55:44.069 --> 00:55:49.700
sing something that, if you slow it down,
it sort of Gregorian chant, where zebra finches

00:55:49.700 --> 00:55:56.940
are rappers. And there's simply no way in
which a canary can sing a zebra finch song.

00:55:56.940 --> 00:56:02.089
They just are ill-equipped.
So cross-fostering experience really run a

00:56:02.089 --> 00:56:07.740
whole lot of differences in hardware that
are insurmountable, right? Like in this particular

00:56:07.740 --> 00:56:13.670
case, you can't have a human baby breathing
underwater. So you can't leave it to dolphins.

00:56:13.670 --> 00:56:24.930
I mean, it's part of the joke, right? But
you really cannot ... There's a limitation

00:56:24.930 --> 00:56:30.849
to how much you can cross-foster across species
that are actually physically distinct.

00:56:30.849 --> 00:56:37.570
So dolphins, for instance, they communicate
in another sound range, some of which we can

00:56:37.570 --> 00:56:44.540
hear, most of which we cannot. They see in
a visual range that, they don't see red, they

00:56:44.540 --> 00:56:50.860
don't see orange. Their vision starts in the
green, and it goes all the way to violet,

00:56:50.860 --> 00:56:57.210
and maybe beyond. And therefore, they see,
naturally, in a different spectral range,

00:56:57.210 --> 00:57:02.250
just like they speak and hear in a different
spectral range. There's nothing innate in

00:57:02.250 --> 00:57:07.660
a human baby that if a human baby is raised
with a species that speaks at a different

00:57:07.660 --> 00:57:10.780
frequency range ... They wouldn't be able
to hear that, because they're ill-equipped

00:57:10.780 --> 00:57:17.440
in the same sense that we will never, no matter
who raises us, we will never see ultraviolet

00:57:17.440 --> 00:57:24.300
or infrared. It just the way our sensors are
encoded. So there's intrinsic limitations

00:57:24.300 --> 00:57:32.460
of how much you can do of this. And because
the physical environment determines so much

00:57:32.460 --> 00:57:39.540
how we perceive the world, our senses are
exquisitely adjusted to our sensory environment,

00:57:39.540 --> 00:57:47.330
and to our evolutionary history. So I don't
think there's anyway to actually do anything

00:57:47.330 --> 00:57:51.700
of the sort.
I just want to jump in on that and say another

00:57:51.700 --> 00:57:57.720
limitation on this kind of thing is that a
lot of linguists think that humans have something

00:57:57.720 --> 00:58:03.670
called universal grammar, which is something
to do with like an innate language faculty.

00:58:03.670 --> 00:58:06.990
Even though languages can be very different,
all human languages have some commonalities

00:58:06.990 --> 00:58:12.800
in their grammar. And in a sense, there's
some part of us, some part of the hard-wiring

00:58:12.800 --> 00:58:19.099
in our brain, that we're the kind of creatures
that are just born knowing how to pick up

00:58:19.099 --> 00:58:22.920
human languages. And then we're immersed in
particular language, and that's why babies

00:58:22.920 --> 00:58:27.869
can learn whatever language that they are
born into. But there's no real reason to think

00:58:27.869 --> 00:58:32.579
that an alien language ... Maybe dolphin language
because at least we have some commonalty,

00:58:32.579 --> 00:58:36.070
I'm not going to speak on dolphins. But there's
no reason to think that an alien language

00:58:36.070 --> 00:58:41.500
is going to share the universal grammar. So
even if we could take one of our human babies,

00:58:41.500 --> 00:58:45.230
all the other concerns notwithstanding, and
send them to live with the aliens, it's not

00:58:45.230 --> 00:58:51.690
clear that a human baby would have the righWSt
kind of brain to even pick up the alien language.

